
CyberShield is a full-stack phishing detection platform I built as an ethical hacking mini-project. Instead of relying on a single method, it layers four independent detection techniques — email header verification (SPF/DKIM/DMARC), URL reputation analysis, WHOIS domain-age reconnaissance, and a TF-IDF + Naive Bayes ML classifier — into one composite 0–100 risk score. The result is a SOC-style dashboard where you paste a suspicious email and get an instant threat report, complete with reasoning, actionable recommendations, and a downloadable PDF. Built with Flask, Scikit-learn, SQLite, and Chart.js.
